      "reasons": [
        "The definition adds that tonic contraction is “a continued, steady state of muscular tightening,” but the packet only states that vaso-constrictor fibres “normally keep [the muscular coats] in a state of tonic contraction,” without explicitly describing it as “continued” or “steady.”",
        "The definition says it “refers especially to… normal maintained narrowing of the small arteries,” but the packet does not explicitly state “narrowing” or “normal maintained narrowing”; it only describes vaso-motor nerves as regulating arterial calibre via innervation and that vaso-constrictor fibres keep the vessel muscular coats in tonic contraction."
